{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836072",
      "title": "Adding & Using Tailwind CSS In A React Project",
      "sourceHash": "d5843746b819a10a12ba5b2eaf99a6a8a51b09585d645abbb51f6c35de8803cc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "So, the nice thing about Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "is that you can customize it if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "There are lots of configuration and customization options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.57,
          "en": "and the official docs are the best place to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.57,
          "end": 13.593,
          "en": "all about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna do two things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 21.453,
          "en": "I wanna bring back my nice background and add a custom font.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.47,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "Now for that, I'll go back to the index CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "And in there we should keep those entries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 33.33,
          "en": "but we can still add our own CSS selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.33,
          "end": 34.98,
          "en": "and rules in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "That's not forbidden just because we're using Tailwind here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 41.52,
          "en": "So, we can still set up our own rules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.52,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "And here I'll, for example, bring back that rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 46.653,
          "en": "which styles my body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 54.5,
          "en": "like this, to bring back that nice background image here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.77,
          "end": 57.81,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to the custom font,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.81,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "I'm still importing a custom font",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 63.393,
          "en": "from Google Fonts in my index HTML file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 66.3,
          "en": "So, that will still be imported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.3,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "even though I'm now using Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "And I can now actually tell Tailwind CSS with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 78.89,
          "en": "of its configuration file, to create a new utility class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 81.273,
          "en": "that allows me to use that custom font.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "For this here in that theme setting under extend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 88.63,
          "en": "we can add the font-family key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "and then register a new font-family",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "with any identifier of our choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "So font-family, this identifier here, is not up to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "This is required to tell Tailwind CSS that we wanna extend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.923,
          "en": "the list of supported fonts it has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 112.14,
          "en": "But now title here, is a new name for a new font",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.14,
          "end": 114.15,
          "en": "that I want to add to Tailwind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.15,
          "end": 117.93,
          "en": "And the value for that is an array where we now need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.93,
          "end": 121.77,
          "en": "to specify the name of our font between double quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.77,
          "end": 123.63,
          "en": "inside of single quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 124.92,
          "en": "It looks a bit strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 127.953,
          "en": "but this is how it's required by Tailwind to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "And then cursive as a fallback maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "And the double quotes are only needed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 138.993,
          "en": "for this special font, which is imported from Google Fonts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "And with this added here, if you save that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 147.063,
          "en": "you can go back and for this title here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.32,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "this h1 element in the header JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 154.5,
          "en": "we can now also add font dash title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.5,
          "end": 157.74,
          "en": "And I'm even getting a suggestion here, as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.74,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "And this font title class is now available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 164.793,
          "en": "because I added this new title font-family to the config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 169.05,
          "en": "And with that, if I save that all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.05,
          "end": 171.09300000000002,
          "en": "you see I got this look here back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.19,
          "end": 175.77,
          "en": "And I can now also improve the look of this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.77,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "by going to the paragraph and giving this a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "of, let's say, text dash stone 500,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 187.203,
          "en": "which is another built-in color I want to use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.91,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "And with that, you see that I have this grayish color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 193.413,
          "en": "back on this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "So, as you can tell by now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.92000000000002,
          "en": "using Tailwind is all about adding utility classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.92000000000002,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "like this and therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 205.23,
          "en": "a potential disadvantage is that we do end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.23,
          "end": 208.743,
          "en": "with long lists of classes like we have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 213.39,
          "en": "And if this is something you absolutely don't like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 216.303,
          "en": "Tailwind might not be the best choice for you.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}